                "The six views that matter most, with two more behind **More measures**. Every figure comes from filed results on Screener, consolidated unless a company now files only standalone accounts (**Cera** since selling its last subsidiaries in September 2025, and **Greenpanel**) or has only a short consolidated history (**Rushil**, from FY25). Two warnings for this group. First, the Q1 FY27 column is lifted for the tile makers by price rises after the Morbi shutdown, and dented for the panel makers by resin costs; the note under each grid says what normal looks like. Second, several companies carry foreign-currency loans, so Screener's operating profit includes forex losses the companies exclude. Hover over a starred name for its caveat.",
